{"items":[{"id":"cap-v2-ordering_and_selection-java-generation-01","problem":"Implement `Solution.java` using only the Java standard library.

Expose this exact API:

`public static List<String> prioritize(String[] requests)`

Each request must have the exact form `name|tier|sequence`, where:
- `name` matches `[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*`.
- `tier` is a decimal integer from 0 through 9.
- `sequence` is a non-negative decimal integer that fits in a Java `long`.

Return the original request strings ordered by tier descending, then sequence ascending, then name in ascending Unicode lexicographic order. Completely identical records must retain their original relative order.

Malformed input must cause an `IllegalArgumentException`. This includes a null array, a null request, the wrong number of fields, an invalid name, a tier outside its permitted range, or an invalid sequence. For an invalid element, the exception message must be `invalid request at index i`, where `i` is its zero-based index. For a null array, use `requests must not be null`.

Do not modify the supplied array. The implementation must be deterministic and must not use the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks. Submit one complete source file containing a public final class named `Solution`.","reference_code":"import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.List;

public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {
    }

    public static List<String> prioritize(String[] requests) {
        if (requests == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("requests must not be null");
        }

        List<Request> parsed = new ArrayList<>(requests.length);
        for (int i = 0; i < requests.length; i++) {
            parsed.add(parse(requests[i], i));
        }

        parsed.sort(Comparator.comparingInt((Request r) -> r.tier).reversed()
                .thenComparingLong(r -> r.sequence)
                .thenComparing(r -> r.name)
                .thenComparingInt(r -> r.index));

        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>(parsed.size());
        for (Request request : parsed) {
            result.add(request.original);
        }
        return result;
    }

    private static Request parse(String text, int index) {
        if (text == null) {
            throw invalid(index);
        }
        String[] fields = text.split("\\|", -1);
        if (fields.length != 3 || !fields[0].matches("[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]*")) {
            throw invalid(index);
        }

        try {
            int tier = Integer.parseInt(fields[1]);
            long sequence = Long.parseLong(fields[2]);
            if (tier < 0 || tier > 9 || sequence < 0) {
                throw invalid(index);
            }
            return new Request(text, fields[0], tier, sequence, index);
        } catch (NumberFormatException ex) {
            throw invalid(index);
        }
    }

    private static IllegalArgumentException invalid(int index) {
        return new IllegalArgumentException("invalid request at index " + index);
    }

    private static final class Request {
        private final String original;
        private final String name;
        private final int tier;
        private final long sequence;
        private final int index;

        private Request(String original, String name, int tier, long sequence, int index) {
            this.original = original;
            this.name = name;
            this.tier = tier;
            this.sequence = sequence;
            this.index = index;
        }
    }
}
