Expose this exact API:

`public static List<String> selectWinners(String[] entries, int limit)`

Each entry must have the exact form `label:score`. A label must match `[a-z][a-z0-9-]*`, and score must be a decimal integer from -1000 through 1000. The colon must occur exactly once.

Select exactly `limit` entries after ranking all entries by score descending, then label in ascending Unicode lexicographic order. If duplicate entries have the same score and label, retain their input order. Return only the labels in ranked order.

A null array, null entry, malformed entry, out-of-range score, or limit outside `0..entries.length` must cause an `IllegalArgumentException`. Use `entries must not be null` for a null array, `invalid limit` for an invalid limit, and `invalid entry at index i` for an invalid element at zero-based index `i`.

Do not modify the supplied array. The implementation must be deterministic and must not use the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks. Submit one complete source file containing a public final class named `Solution`.","reference_code":"import java.util.ArrayList;
import java.util.Comparator;
import java.util.List;

public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {
    }

    public static List<String> selectWinners(String[] entries, int limit) {
        if (entries == null) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("entries must not be null");
        }
        if (limit < 0 || limit > entries.length) {
            throw new IllegalArgumentException("invalid limit");
        }

        List<Entry> ranked = new ArrayList<>(entries.length);
        for (int i = 0; i < entries.length; i++) {
            ranked.add(parse(entries[i], i));
        }

        ranked.sort(Comparator.comparingInt((Entry e) -> e.score).reversed()
                .thenComparing(e -> e.label)
                .thenComparingInt(e -> e.index));

        List<String> result = new ArrayList<>(limit);
        for (int i = 0; i < limit; i++) {
            result.add(ranked.get(i).label);
        }
        return result;
    }

    private static Entry parse(String text, int index) {
        if (text == null) {
            throw invalid(index);
        }
        int colon = text.indexOf(':');
        if (colon <= 0 || colon != text.lastIndexOf(':')) {
            throw invalid(index);
        }

        String label = text.substring(0, colon);
        String scoreText = text.substring(colon + 1);
        if (!label.matches("[a-z][a-z0-9-]*") || scoreText.isEmpty()) {
            throw invalid(index);
        }

        try {
            int score = Integer.parseInt(scoreText);
            if (score < -1000 || score > 1000) {
                throw invalid(index);
            }
            return new Entry(label, score, index);
        } catch (NumberFormatException ex) {
            throw invalid(index);
        }
    }

    private static IllegalArgumentException invalid(int index) {
        return new IllegalArgumentException("invalid entry at index " + index);
    }

    private static final class Entry {
        private final String label;
        private final int score;
        private final int index;

        private Entry(String label, int score, int index) {
            this.label = label;
            this.score = score;
            this.index = index;
        }
    }
}
