","known_bad_label":"Takes from the right array first on equal values, violating the specified stable merge precedence."},{"id":"cap-v2-parsing_and_encoding-java-generation-01","problem":"Implement `Solution.java` using only the Java standard library.

Expose this exact API:

`public static String[] normalizeRecords(String[] records)`

Each input record is independently interpreted as a semicolon-separated sequence of `key=value` fields. The empty string represents a record with no fields. Keys contain one or more lowercase ASCII letters. Values are sequences of tokens, where each token is either an unreserved character from `[A-Za-z0-9._-]` or a percent escape `%HH`. `HH` consists of two hexadecimal digits and represents one printable ASCII character from code 32 through 126.

Within one record, a later occurrence of a key replaces its earlier value. Produce one canonical string per input record by sorting its surviving keys lexicographically and joining their `key=value` fields with semicolons. Decode escapes before applying replacement, then encode each value canonically: unreserved characters appear literally and every other character appears as `%HH` using uppercase hexadecimal digits.

Records must be state-isolated. Fields parsed from one array element must never appear in or affect another element, even when a later record is empty or omits those keys. Inputs conform to the grammar above.

Do not modify the supplied array. The implementation must be deterministic and must not use the filesystem, network, clock, randomness, external packages, or frameworks. Submit one complete source file containing a public final class named `Solution`.","reference_code":"import java.util.Map;
import java.util.TreeMap;

public final class Solution {
    private Solution() {
    }

    public static String[] normalizeRecords(String[] records) {
        String[] result = new String[records.length];

        for (int i = 0; i < records.length; i++) {
            Map<String, String> fields = new TreeMap<>();
            if (!records[i].isEmpty()) {
                String[] parts = records[i].split(";", -1);
                for (String part : parts) {
                    int equals = part.indexOf('=');
                    String key = part.substring(0, equals);
                    String value = decode(part.substring(equals + 1));
                    fields.put(key, value);
                }
            }
            result[i] = encodeRecord(fields);
        }
        return result;
    }

    private static String decode(String encoded) {
        StringBuilder decoded = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < encoded.length();) {
            char current = encoded.charAt(i);
            if (current == '%') {
                int value = Character.digit(encoded.charAt(i + 1), 16) * 16
                        + Character.digit(encoded.charAt(i + 2), 16);
                decoded.append((char) value);
                i += 3;
            } else {
                decoded.append(current);
                i++;
            }
        }
        return decoded.toString();
    }

    private static String encodeRecord(Map<String, String> fields) {
        StringBuilder output = new StringBuilder();
        for (Map.Entry<String, String> field : fields.entrySet()) {
            if (output.length() > 0) {
                output.append(';');
            }
            output.append(field.getKey()).append('=').append(encode(field.getValue()));
        }
        return output.toString();
    }

    private static String encode(String value) {
        StringBuilder encoded = new StringBuilder();
        for (int i = 0; i < value.length(); i++) {
            char c = value.charAt(i);
            if (isUnreserved(c)) {
                encoded.append(c);
            } else {
                encoded.append('%');
                encoded.append(toHex(c >>> 4));
                encoded.append(toHex(c & 15));
            }
        }
        return encoded.toString();
    }

    private static boolean isUnreserved(char c) {
        return c >= 'A' && c <= 'Z'
                || c >= 'a' && c <= 'z'
                || c >= '0' && c <= '9'
                || c == '.' || c == '_' || c == '-';
    }

    private static char toHex(int value) {
        return "0123456789ABCDEF".charAt(value);
    }
}
